;;; M1a — D2's second shape: `sorted(alive)` over two `Fact` args.
;;;
;;; `mixed-type-hypothesis.ein` is the str-vs-int reproducer Q-M1a.4 was
;;; written about. This is the *other* half of the same hazard, which
;;; [design/02](../../plans/m1a_rust/design/02_determinism_and_order.md) §5 H2
;;; named in one clause — "and a `Fact` has no `__lt__` at all" — and which no
;;; fixture covered until the S1a.6.6 fuzzer produced it:
;;;
;;;     ein.py  TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'Fact' and 'Fact'
;;;     ein.rs  answers (`Value` is totally ordered: Int < Sym < Fact)
;;;
;;; **It needs no mixed slot types.** One hrule whose `:assert` head is a
;;; `(not …)` is enough — the hypothesis's argument is then a nested fact, and
;;; two of them reach `apriori.layer_1`'s `sorted(alive)`. That is an ordinary
;;; puzzle idiom, so D2's reach is wider than its first fixture suggested.
;;; What stays true is the *scope* claim: blind generation still cannot get
;;; here (its candidates are built from `kb.names`, all strings), so an
;;; `(hrule …)` remains necessary.
;;;
;;; Group `crash-parity`: compared on exit code + exception class, never on
;;; the message, which names its operands in a hash-seed-dependent order.

(is-a o1 T)
(is-a o2 T)

(hrule hyp-0 ()
  :match  (is-a ?v0 T)
  :assert (not (r0 ?v0 o2)))
